{% comment %}
  sections/home-services.liquid
  Ported from the "Arcane Flame Website Prototype" option-c.html:
    - CSS: lines ~227-264 (.svc, .svc__card, .svc__card:hover, .svc__frame,
      .svc__badge + children, .svc__card img, .svc--resin img, .svc--fdm img,
      .svc__card::after, .svc__body, .svc__card h3, .svc__card p, .tags,
      .tags span, .svc__link, .svc__link .arw) plus the .svc-relevant slice
      of the <=680px responsive rule (line ~397) — see
      shopify-theme/assets/home-services.css for the full colour-
      substitution notes.
    - Markup: lines ~554-597 (<section class="sec sec--mid" id="services">
      ...</section>) — the "Two ways to print" heading block (including the
      upload-clarity sub-heading added this session) and the two service
      cards (each with the dashed .svc__frame overlay and solid
      .svc__badge added this session).

  ** This section exists specifically to fix a user-flagged confusion **
  (screenshotted twice): without the badge/frame/sub-heading, the two
  photographed models read as a shop catalogue of pre-made products
  rather than examples of customer-uploaded files. Per the task brief,
  three elements are therefore HARDCODED directly in this file, not
  exposed as block/section settings a merchant could edit away:
    1. The section sub-heading line ("Examples from files customers have
       sent us — upload your own STL below and we'll price it the same
       way.") under the eyebrow/heading.
    2. The .svc__frame dashed border overlay on each card (always
       rendered, unconditional — not a toggle).
    3. The .svc__badge "Uploaded STL / not a stock model" badge + upload
       icon on each card (always rendered, unconditional — not a toggle).
  Everything else per card (eyebrow, heading, body, image, tags, CTA
  text/url) is a `service_card` block setting so a merchant can edit
  copy, swap photos or add a third material without a code deploy.

  Judgment call — tags field: the brief allows either a second nested
  block type or a delimited text setting parsed with `| split`. Shopify
  block settings cannot themselves contain a repeating sub-list (blocks
  can't nest inside a block's own settings), so a second block type would
  live as siblings of `service_card` at the section level and have to be
  manually associated back to the right card (fragile, easy for a
  merchant to misorder). Went with a single-line comma-separated `text`
  setting (`tags`, e.g. "32mm heroic, 12K detail, Primed or raw") parsed
  with `| split: ','` in the loop below — one field per card, matches the
  source's 2-3 short tags, and merchants edit a plain text field instead
  of managing extra blocks.
{% endcomment %}
<section class="sec sec--mid" id="Services-{{ section.id }}">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="sec__head">
      <p class="eyebrow reveal">{{ section.settings.eyebrow }}</p>
      <h2 class="display reveal" data-d="1">{{ section.settings.heading }}</h2>
      {% comment %} Hardcoded clarifying sub-line — see file header. Not a section setting. {% endcomment %}
      <p class="lede reveal" data-d="1" style="margin-top:14px">
        Examples from files customers have sent us. <strong style="color:var(--af-white)">Upload your own STL
        below</strong> and we'll price it the same way.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="svc">
      {% for block in section.blocks %}
        {% if block.type == 'service_card' %}
          {% comment %}
            The source's two fixed cards use .svc--resin / .svc--fdm modifier
            classes purely to give each example photo its own absolute
            crop/position (different aspect ratios). With blocks now
            merchant-editable, alternate the same two positioning variants by
            index (odd/even) rather than hardcoding "resin"/"fdm" — see
            home-services.css for what each variant actually controls.
          {% endcomment %}
          {% assign card_variant = 'a' %}
          {% assign card_index_remainder = forloop.index0 | modulo: 2 %}
          {% if card_index_remainder == 1 %}
            {% assign card_variant = 'b' %}
          {% endif %}
          <article class="svc__card svc--{{ card_variant }} reveal" {% if forloop.index0 > 0 %}data-d="1"{% endif %} {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
            {% comment %} Hardcoded dashed frame overlay — see file header. Not a block setting. {% endcomment %}
            <div class="svc__frame"></div>
            {% comment %} Hardcoded upload-clarity badge — see file header. Not a block setting. {% endcomment %}
            <span class="svc__badge">
              <svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8"><path d="M21 15v4a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2v-4"/><path d="m7 10 5-5 5 5"/><path d="M12 5v13"/></svg>
              <span>Uploaded STL<br /><em>not a stock model</em></span>
            </span>
            {% if block.settings.image %}
              <img
                src="{{ block.settings.image | image_url: width: 800 }}"
                srcset="{{ block.settings.image | image_url: width: 400 }} 400w, {{ block.settings.image | image_url: width: 800 }} 800w"
                alt="{{ block.settings.image.alt | default: block.settings.heading }}"
                loading="lazy"
                width="{{ block.settings.image.width }}"
                height="{{ block.settings.image.height }}"
              />
            {% endif %}
            <div class="svc__body">
              <p class="eyebrow">{{ block.settings.eyebrow }}</p>
              <h3>{{ block.settings.heading }}</h3>
              {% comment %}
                block.settings.body is a `richtext` setting — Shopify already
                wraps its rendered value in <p>...</p>, so wrapping it in
                another <p> here would produce invalid nested <p><p>...</p></p>
                markup (browsers auto-close unpredictably). Use a <div> instead,
                matching the pattern home-craft.liquid established for its own
                richtext `body` field. Named .svc__body-text rather than
                reusing the shared .lede class, since .lede's 19px/max-width
                sizing doesn't match this card's 15px body-copy treatment —
                see home-services.css for the matching selector.
              {% endcomment %}
              <div class="svc__body-text">{{ block.settings.body }}</div>
              {% if block.settings.tags != blank %}
                <div class="tags">
                  {% assign tag_list = block.settings.tags | split: ',' %}
                  {% for tag in tag_list %}
                    <span>{{ tag | strip }}</span>
                  {% endfor %}
                </div>
              {% endif %}
              {% if block.settings.cta_text != blank %}
                <a href="{{ block.settings.cta_url }}" class="svc__link">{{ block.settings.cta_text }} <span class="arw">→</span></a>
              {% endif %}
            </div>
          </article>
        {% endif %}
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

